$$
\Delta T = \frac{Q}{mc} = \frac{2.94 \times 10^5}{2 \times 4.2 \times 10^3} = 35^\circ\text{C}
$$  
The final temperature is $ 55^\circ\text{C} $, so the initial temperature $ [X] $ is:  
$$
X = 55^\circ\text{C} - 35^\circ\text{C} = 20^\circ\text{C}
$$  
Final answer: \boxed{20°C}

